WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.350
Groups and service accounts each get
one recorded decision per object.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:10.587
Entra ID has no group scope, so the classic
AD nesting model doesn't map one to one.

3
00:00:10.587 --> 00:00:14.851
Every security group gets one of
five outcomes: keep it in AD,

4
00:00:14.851 --> 00:00:19.113
sync it, convert it to cloud-only,
make it dynamic, or retire it.

5
00:00:19.113 --> 00:00:23.842
Nesting also works for fewer things
in Entra ID, since app assignment and

6
00:00:23.842 --> 00:00:28.413
licensing don't cascade, so flatten
deep chains and record the mapping.

7
00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:32.513
For service accounts, the rule
is to eliminate stored secrets.

8
00:00:32.513 --> 00:00:37.203
Accounts that call cloud APIs become
app registrations with certificates or

9
00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:41.100
federated credentials, Azure
workloads get managed identities,

10
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.501
and on-premises Kerberos workloads go
to group managed service accounts.

11
00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:50.060
Every app gets two human owners,
and no client secrets in production.
